  "chapter": {
    "number": 47,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(48) A Psalm of",
          {
            "noteId": 87
          },
          "praise for the sons of Core on the second day of the week."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Great is the Lord, and greatly to be praised in the city of our God, in his holy mountain.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The city of the great King is well planted on the mountains of Sion, with the joy of the whole earth, on the sides of the north.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "God is known in her palaces, when he undertakes to help her.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For, behold the kings of the earth were assembled, they came together.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They saw, and so they wondered: they were troubled, they were moved.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Trembling took hold on them: there were the pangs as of a woman in travail.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You will break the ships of Tharsis with a vehement wind.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "As we have heard, so have we also seen, in the city of the Lord of hosts, in the city of our God: God has founded it for ever. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "We have thought of your mercy, O God, in the midst of your people.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "According to your name, O God, so is also your praise to the ends of the earth: your right hand is full of righteousness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let mount Sion rejoice, let the daughters of Judaea exult, because of your judgments, O Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Go round about Sion, and encompass her: tell you⌃ her towers.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Mark you⌃ well her strength, and observe her palaces; that you⌃ may tell the next generation.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For this is our God for ever and ever: he will be our guide for evermore.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 87,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "A song.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 47,
          "verse": 0
        }
      }
    ]
